---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import VideoThumbnail from "@/components/concerts/VideoThumbnail.astro";
import VideoModal from "@/components/concerts/VideoModal.astro";
import Text from "@/components/typography/Text.astro";
import miniGole from "@/assets/bio/mini-gole.png";
import classmates from "@/assets/images/classmates.jpg";
---

<PageLayout
  heading="Bio"
  description="A personal journal by Manish Tamang (golecodes)."
>
  <section class="grid items-start gap-8 sm:grid-cols-[1fr_auto]">
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <Text>
        Since childhood, I have been driven by curiosity and a deep passion for
        learning. I have always been eager to explore new ideas and understand
        how things work, often looking at them from different perspectives.
      </Text>
      <Text>
        I am naturally drawn to minimalism and clarity, preferring simplicity
        over anything cluttered or messy. From the very beginning, I have
        carried a positive mindset toward growth, always seeking to learn,
        improve, and see the bigger picture.
      </Text>
    </div>

    <!-- Name card: the caption slides up on hover -->
    <figure
      class="group relative h-48 w-40 overflow-hidden rounded-lg justify-self-center sm:justify-self-end"
    >
      <Image
        src={miniGole}
        alt="Manish Tamang as a kid"
        width={160}
        densities={[1, 2]}
        draggable="false"
        class="size-full object-cover opacity-90 select-none"
      />
      <figcaption
        class="absolute inset-x-0 -bottom-16 flex flex-col gap-1 bg-subtle p-2 transition-[bottom] duration-500 group-hover:bottom-0"
      >
        <span class="font-display text-lg text-link">Manish Gole</span>
        <span class="text-xs text-muted-foreground"
          >My friends also call me Gole.</span
        >
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <div class="mt-10 space-y-4">
    <Text>
      I was born in Bhojpur, Nepal, in 2008. I moved to Itahari for school, then
      to Kathmandu after the 6th grade, and later back to Itahari for my +2. Now
      I'm in Kathmandu again, working on small client projects, freelancing, and
      trying to figure out the next few years.
    </Text>
    <Text>
      In the 6th grade I saw QBasic on a projector for the first time, and that
      was it. I knew I wanted to go toward computers. In 7th and 8th grade, my
      computer teacher, Nishan sir, made the basics feel easy, and I loved
      solving QBasic problems.
    </Text>
    <Text>
      My web journey started in 9th grade, around 2021–2022. My new computer
      teacher at Prashanti Academy, Millan Sunuwar Rawacha sir (<a
        href="https://www.youtube.com/@millan.977"
        class="text-link hover:underline">his YouTube channel</a
      >), saw some potential in me and asked, why not build a website for the
      school? I said, why not, I can do anything.
    </Text>
    <Text>
      I went home to my brother's Acer laptop. All I knew was that a website is
      a collection of web pages, and I only knew how to make one in Notepad. I
      never thought about hosting. A few days later I showed him my page on a
      pen drive. He liked it, but said it wasn't a real task yet: now host it
      and make it public.
    </Text>
    <Text>
      I had no idea what that meant, so I did some research, found Netlify, and
      put my first site online under my own name at <a
        href="https://manishtamang.netlify.app/"
        class="text-link hover:underline">manishtamang.netlify.app</a
      >. More of that time is in <a
        href="/blog/my-personal-journey-with-prashanti-academy-a-tale-of-growth-and-gratitude"
        class="text-link hover:underline">my Prashanti Academy post</a
      >.
    </Text>
    <Text>
      After that I wanted to build dynamic sites. I spent almost six months on
      PHP because it was trending, then found Next.js and left PHP behind. I
      still couldn't make a properly dynamic site, until I learned about CMSs
      and started building with Sanity. They even sent me some merch: a t-shirt
      in 2023 and a sweatshirt in 2024.
    </Text>
    <div class="my-8 grid items-start gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <figure>
      <Image
        src={classmates}
        alt="Ten classmates in school uniform posing together in a classroom with teal walls"
        widths={[320, 480, 640]}
        sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 360px"
        quality={78}
        class="w-full rounded-lg border border-border"
      />
      <figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        Photo with boys, Sushma godawari college
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure>
      <VideoThumbnail
        src="https://shhe8ako63pfhxto.public.blob.vercel-storage.com/video_20250904_web.mp4"
        label="Preparation of the welcome program, Sep 4, 2025"
        caption="Preparation of the welcome program, Sep 4, 2025"
        wide
      />
      <figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        Video clicked on Sep 4, 2025, preparation of the welcome program
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    </div>
    <Text>
      The journey is still going. I make minimal sites, freelance, and build
      projects. I've earned a bit along the way, and I'm still learning and
      working out what I'm for, and what's next.
    </Text>
  </div>
  <VideoModal />
</PageLayout>
